[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Azzurro
GenericName=BluOS Controller
Comment=Control BluOS players — Bluesound, NAD and PSB
Exec=azzurro
Icon=blue.azzurro.Azzurro
Terminal=false
Categories=AudioVideo;Audio;Player;
Keywords=BluOS;Bluesound;NAD;PSB;music;multiroom;speaker;streaming;
# The X11 window class, which is the application id, the same as the Wayland
# app_id. slint::set_xdg_app_id sets both: Slint hands the id to winit as the
# window's class name, and winit writes it into WM_CLASS. Checked with xprop:
# WM_CLASS(STRING) = "", "blue.azzurro.Azzurro" — the empty string is the
# instance name, which Slint leaves blank. Under Wayland the app_id is the same
# string, so the shell finds this file either by this key or by its own name.
#
# It said "azzurro" at first, from an xprop taken while set_xdg_app_id was still
# failing silently, called before any backend had been selected (see run_app).
# winit falls back to the binary's name for a window with no class of its own,
# which is where that value came from; once the call succeeded, it matched no
# window at all.
StartupWMClass=blue.azzurro.Azzurro
